  "notes": "{指|さ}す is a godan verb meaning to point at or indicate something.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Takes ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ particle for the target\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦{指|ゆび}→指：01518_yubi⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{指|さ}す: to point with a finger\n- 〜⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{指|さ}す: to refer to ~, indicate ~\n- ⟦{方向|ほうこう}→方向：03617_houkou⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{指|さ}す: to point in a direction\n- ⟦{針|はり}→針：03566_hari⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{北|きた}→北：00644_kita⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{指|さ}す: needle points north\n\nHOMOPHONES (different kanji):\n- ⟦{差|さ}す→差す：17637_sasu⟧: to hold up (umbrella), shine through\n- ⟦{刺|さ}す→刺す：02111_sasu⟧: to stab, pierce, sting\n- ⟦{挿|さ}す→挿す：02466_sasu⟧: to insert\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nPointing directly at people with a finger is considered rude in Japan.",
